Description: Implements Claim-Scoped Diagnostic Gates (CSDG) for planning,
    executing, documenting, and exporting diagnostics for interpretable
    machine-learning analyses. The package integrates with the 'mlr3'
    ecosystem and separates predictive performance, measurement and
    preprocessing review, proposition and six-coordinate context comparison, orthogonal evidence
    roles, non-compensatory claim adjudication, dependence and support,
    calibration, local faithfulness, explanation stability, model and setting
    generalization, and subgroup auditing. The existing AutoIML workflow
    remains available for compatibility. Legacy pass/warn/fail labels are
    quarantined from CSDG claim decisions. CSDG applies no aggregate score,
    readiness grade, or universal substantive threshold.
